### Description

Initiate an approval for enabling or disabling a cron job. This API only creates an approval task and runs a full pre-check on the parameters. **The cron job status is not changed.** Once the approval is granted, Job changes it automatically as the creator of the task.

Before calling: the target cron job must exist in the given resource scope and the caller must have the permission to enable or disable cron jobs in that scope. If the pre-check fails, an error is returned and no approval task is created.

{% include '_generic_v4_approval_flow.md.j2' %}

### Request Parameters

#### Body Parameters

| Field | Type | Required | Description |
|-------|------|----------|-------------|
| bk_scope_type | string | Yes | Resource scope type. Options: `biz` (business), `biz_set` (business set) |
| bk_scope_id | string | Yes | Resource scope ID, corresponding to `bk_scope_type`, that is the business ID or the business set ID |
| approval_channel | string | No | Approval channel. Options: `IMATE` (IMate approval channel). The default channel configured on the server is used when omitted. Only the channel enum can be specified; the channel address and secret always come from the server configuration |
| id | long | Yes | Cron job ID |
| status | int | Yes | Target status. Options: 1 (start), 2 (pause) |

### Request Parameters Example

- POST

```json
{
    "bk_scope_type": "biz",
    "bk_scope_id": "2",
    "approval_channel": "IMATE",
    "id": 700001,
    "status": 1
}
```

